# Cursor/Claude doc sync

When updating guidance, commands, skills, or workflow documentation, keep Cursor and Claude docs aligned in the same change.

- Treat `.cursor/**` and `.claude/**` guidance docs as mirrored sources of truth.
- If you add or modify a command, rule, or workflow in one ecosystem, update the corresponding doc in the other ecosystem in the same task.
- Keep intent, behavior, and operational steps identical unless a platform-specific difference is explicitly required.
- If a platform-specific difference is required, document the reason directly in both docs.
- Do not leave one side partially updated; complete both updates before considering the task done.
- **Agent workflow** (worktrees, frontiers, **subagents / context budget** in **`docs/ai-context.md` §1b**) must stay aligned across **`docs/ai-context.md`** (and **`docs/ai-context.project.md`** when it exists), **`.cursor/rules/main.mdc`**, **`.claude/rules/development-standards.md`**, **`CLAUDE.md`** (and **`CLAUDE.project.md`** when it exists), and any **`.cursor/skills/`** or **`.claude/commands/`** files that restate those rules.
- **Docs authority** (design as source of truth, escalation tags, fix-code-not-docs) must stay aligned across **`docs/ai-context.md`**, **`docs/ai-context.project.md`** when it amends process authority, **`docs/design/documentation-style.md`**, **`.cursor/rules/docs-authority-and-escalation.mdc`**, and **`.claude/rules/docs-authority-and-escalation.md`**.
- **Project overlays (`*.project.*`):** Repo-specific process text that must survive **`./sync-skeleton`** belongs in **`NAME.project.EXT`** beside the synced base file (see **`docs/skeleton-project-overlays.md`**). When you change **template-wide** wording for all consumers, edit the base **`docs/ai-context.md`** / **`CLAUDE.md`** in **`.skeleton/`** (or the synced root copies) and mirror Cursor/Claude rules in the same change; when you change **one-repo** behavior, edit the **`.project.`** file and any **`.cursor`** / **`.claude`** mirrors together per the bullets above.
